  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their `default_map` entries again. The bug was in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py:392`.\n\nA subcommand context inherited its parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own name. A map like `{\"sub\": {\"opt\": 1}}` was therefore looked up as `opt` at the top level and never matched. The line is now `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\nThe test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't add a regression test for the nested-subcommand case.",
